 # Data Cache
+
+Library cover view uses three columns and nine books per page, sharing Home’s cover component and sizing. A low-priority worker creates EPUB/XTC thumbnails without accessing the renderer or input loop, prioritizing the visible page and then continuing through other pages while idle. Only one copied job is retained; thumbnails live in the existing per-book SD caches. In-progress BMP files are never painted. Library filtering processes one source book between input checks after the first paint. Books without covers use a placeholder; confirmed missing EPUB covers are remembered in `library-cover-missing`. Text files use a placeholder. Library opens the saved index on startup. After its first paint, a paced metadata-only check compares book paths, sizes, and modification timestamps with the saved index, then offers Refresh if they differ. Transfers and on-device file changes also offer Refresh. The check reads no book contents; edits retaining both size and timestamp may not be detected. No rebuild occurs until Refresh is selected unless the index is missing or incompatible. No cache format change or cache deletion is needed.

 CrossInk caches data aggressively on the SD card to minimize RAM use. The ESP32-C3 has about 380 KB of usable RAM, so rebuilding every book structure in memory on every open would be too expensive.

@@ -136,3 +138,19 @@

 The Lyra Carousel snapshot cache advances to version 7 so cached home menus
 regenerate with the Library label and landmark icon. No manual EPUB cache reset is required.
+
+## Library view snapshots
+
+`library-filter.cache` and `library-recents.cache` store completed filter membership
+and counts. Keys include the query, sort/direction, file filters, metadata preference,
+completion filter, and index header or recent-history contents. They do not contain
+book text or images. Index rebuilds/file changes and completion changes invalidate
+both snapshots; ordinary reading-time/page-count saves do not. A cold or invalid
+snapshot falls back to the existing incremental filter and is replaced on completion.
+Rendered cover pixels use the same optional PSRAM cache as Home. The first completed
+visible cover batch repaints once; later idle preloading does not repaint the screen.
+Sorting and reverse order are in the cover-view menu. Count and page share one footer;
+status changes do not resize the grid and trigger another thumbnail-size conversion.
+“Refresh covers on this page” removes the current nine thumbnails and negative-cover
+markers, resets their pixel slots, and prepares fresh images without rebuilding the
+library index or clearing saved filter counts. Missing images display the title.
